From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] hdmitx21: honour the user_attr range on the VPU_HDMI matrix
 chips

S1A, S7, and S7D/S6 with CSC_type yuv2rgb, make RGB with the VPU_HDMI
ycbcr2rgb matrix. Stock always loads BT.601 limited YCbCr to full range
RGB while the AVI infoframe says Q = limited: full range pixels labelled
limited, with a 601 hue error on HD and BT.2020. No use to a meter.

vpu_hdmi_set_matrix_ycbcr2rgb() becomes the one writer, from a table. For
a user_attr format it loads the 601, 709 or 2020 matrix the AVI declares,
in the requested range (limited adds the 64 offset); otherwise it writes
the stock values. It also runs when the AVI colorimetry changes without a
mode set (CONF_AVI_BT2020), skipping a matrix already loaded; the
rgb2ycbcr writer invalidates that record. The AVI send path only sets Q,
and YQ to limited, with no register access. The Dolby Vision tunnel keeps
the stock matrix. These chips set user_range_cap, so full is accepted.

Without user_attr every register write, value and log line is stock. The
coefficient slots are inferred from the stock 601 values; a meter reading
of 100% red in 709 and 2020 checks them. Built against the pinned tree,
not run on hardware.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
